Add a module-level normaliser above grade_quiz:
  def _flatten_questions(content):
      if isinstance(content, dict):
          return list(content.get("multiple_choice") or []) + list(content.get("short_answer") or [])
      return content if isinstance(content, list) else []
In grade_quiz replace lines 178-185 with:
  parsed_content = _flatten_questions(json.loads(m.content) if isinstance(m.content, str) else m.content)
In list_study_decks (line 64) apply `parsed = _flatten_questions(parsed)` before total_cards and before the "cards" field (line 88). Mirror the flattening in server/routes_library.py:_serialize_material (lines 14-18) when kind == 'practice_test' so /api/library/materials also returns a list.

Replace the single-click mastery rule at line 120 with a real threshold:
  interval = review_res.get("interval_days", 0)
  if payload.rating == 1:
      new_state = "learning"
  elif payload.rating >= 3 and interval >= 21 and (card_state.reps if hasattr(card_state, "reps") else 0) >= 2:
